Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-04-2001||10:52 AM||||Doesnt the spoiler and the fastback quarter windows hinder backing up though?  I can see very well at night backing up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||06-04-2001||03:27 PM||||I think the green backup lights are a go with the glowing pedals. Maybe they include some free stickers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||Jaei Sun||06-04-2001||07:23 PM||||I had the same trouble backing up at night of not being able to see enough of the area behind me...  thanks to GM deciding to tint the plastic of the taillights.<P>So I did the DXR mod and put in these lil' babies... 50 watt halogen each, so when I back up I have all four going and I can see everything!<P> <IMG SRC="http://jaeisfieropix.50megs.com/backup_mod.jpg"> <P>And if I want I can drop in some hyperwhite halogens in to get a nice different look.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||TRiAD||06-04-2001||07:26 PM||||Jaei Sun, what are those lights?<BR>Could you let us all in?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||CoolBlue87GT||06-04-2001||09:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>50 watt halogen each, so when I back up I have all four going and I can see everything!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>That's pretty neat !  That's a really good idea.<P>I guess you could use those for tailgaters also !!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||06-04-2001||09:21 PM||||[So I did the DXR mod and put in these lil' babies... 50 watt halogen each, so when I back up I have all four going and I can see everything!<BR>[/B][/QUOTE]<BR>The only problem I see is now there is a lack of rear reflectors. So parked or broken on the side of the road at night might be bad.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||06-04-2001||09:52 PM||||Well, I dont know about MN plates but my MI plates have a reflective band in them that will shine pretty good when headlights hit it.  Its nothing like the regular red reflectors, but it still is something.<P>I dont know if it would be possible to add reflectors in there anywhere or not.  If you are worried about not being seen while broken down at night, get some flares I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jaei Sun||06-04-2001||11:55 PM||||The lights are made by Pilot, they're called Navigators.  DXR_DAD was the original person who did them.  As far as the reflective material goes, FieroJoe is right the MN plates have reflective material too,  And the lights themselves are chromed on the inside and reflect light pretty well too.<P>In the future I'm getting my black trim painted white and there is this 3m reflective tape that looks white from a distance and I'll be putting a strip of it across the back so it will blend in with the paint.<P>But for the other folks you probably could crack open your taillight lens and put some reflective red lenses or tape inside under the clear lens covers.... just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||4
